# ai_tools_dotnet file contexts: the .NET output layout inside a SANDBOX CLONE. Clones are
# labelled by the static rule in ai_tools.fc plus a plain restorecon (no per-clone semanage
# rule, no root), so the build-output directories inside one need a static rule of their own,
# and it lives in the integration's layout module because the names are the integration's: the
# same set as the type transitions in ai_tools_dotnet.te, which states the coupling. Keyed under
# /opt for the same reason the clone rule in ai_tools.fc is: file_contexts.subs_dist aliases
# /var/opt to /opt before matching. A claimed project under a home gets the equivalent rule per
# project from relabel.lib.sh, from the same names in the manifest.
#
# Precedence: this rule and the clone rule in ai_tools.fc share a stem (the literal prefix
# before the first metacharacter), and among equal stems the later, longer regex is the
# match, so a path under bin/, obj/ or artifacts/ resolves here and every other clone path to
# the clone rule. Verify on a host with the module loaded, since this is the property the
# narrowing rests on:
#   matchpathcon /var/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/x/src/p/bin/y   (expect ai_tools_project_build_t)
#   matchpathcon /var/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/x/.githooks/h   (expect ai_tools_project_t)
/opt/ai-tools/sandbox-projects/[^/]+(/.*)?/(bin|obj|artifacts)(/.*)?  gen_context(system_u:object_r:ai_tools_project_build_t,s0)
